  [1mModules[0m, each independently testable:

  ┌─────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │   Module    │           Responsibility           │                 Depends on                  │
  ├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mstore.js[39m    │ load/save tasks, localStorage only │ nothing                                     │
  ├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mdueState.js[39m │ pure date logic                    │ nothing                                     │
  ├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mrender.js[39m   │ tasks + due states → DOM           │ nothing (takes data, returns/patches nodes) │
  ├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mapp.js[39m      │ wires events to store and render   │ all three                                   │
  └─────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  The reason for that split: [38;5;153mdueState.js[39m has zero dependencies and holds all the interesting logic, so the risky part of
  this app is testable with plain function calls and no DOM.

  [1mRecompute on load and on a timer[0m — a task due today becomes overdue at midnight, so we re-derive periodically rather
  than only on mutation, or a tab left open overnight shows stale state.

